Description: Write the session history at shutdown before the shell's actors are destroyed.
 The time limits manager blocks shutdown until its session history file has been written, in a nested main loop which
 dispatches whatever arrives meanwhile. GNOME Shell connects its shutdown handler after the one of the layout manager,
 which destroys uiGroup, so signal handlers which outlive their actors run on destroyed ones: installed-changed of
 Shell.AppSystem reaches the app grid, the search view and the date menu's sections, the date menu's weather client,
 calendar event source, world clocks settings and wall clocks reach the date menu, and updated of Main.sessionMode
 reaches popup menus, quick settings toggles, the screenshot UI, the message tray and the calendar. GJS then logs
 "has been already disposed" criticals, which fail the closeWithActiveWindows test now and then. The patch connects
 the handler before the layout manager is created, and the handler returns when the time limits manager does not
 exist yet.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-06

--- a/js/ui/main.js
+++ b/js/ui/main.js
@@ -230,6 +230,26 @@
 
     new AnimationsSettings();
 
+    // Block shutdown until the session history file has been written. The
+    // nested main loop for that dispatches whatever arrives meanwhile, so this
+    // is connected before the layout manager connects its shutdown handler,
+    // which destroys uiGroup, to run while the actors still exist.
+    global.connect('shutdown', () => {
+        if (!timeLimitsManager)
+            return;
+
+        const loop = new GLib.MainLoop(null, false);
+        const source = GLib.idle_source_new();
+        source.set_callback(() => {
+            timeLimitsManager.shutdown()
+                .catch(e => console.warn(`Failed to stop time limits manager: ${e.message}`))
+                .finally(() => loop.quit());
+            return GLib.SOURCE_REMOVE;
+        });
+        source.attach(loop.get_context());
+        loop.run();
+    });
+
     // Setup the stage hierarchy early
     layoutManager = new Layout.LayoutManager();
 
